/*!
\page p_forward_declaring Forward Declaring Math Types

Often, to reduce dependencies and to improve build times, users will forward declare types.  We have seen many users
write forward declarations for math types.  Unfortunately, due to the complexity of the math types, it is easy to make
errors when forward declaring them.  Also, forward declarations may need to be updated if math types are modified in
the future.  For these reasons, we highly recommend that instead of manually forward declaring types, you make use
of a type forwarding header provided by the math library.

Just include <tt>rw/math/types_fwd.h</tt> to include forward declarations for all the math types.

*/
